{"affected_obligations":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1","S2","R1"],"proposal":null,"reason":"A faithful executable contract is outside the registered frontend. The required JSON edge arrays contain heterogeneous positional values, and output entries are integers, null, or the exact string \"-inf\". The available typed AST sorts and registered bridge do not specify faithful encodings for these observable JSON structures. Replacing them with records or Except values would require an explicitly registered serialization mapping. The frontend also lacks registered execution-effect and dependency checks for the Python guarantees. Opaque Lean declarations cannot satisfy the required executable Python test campaign. The Lean source supplies no substitute contract or acceptance claim.","required_extensions":["Registered heterogeneous positional JSON edge-array encoding preserving [u,v,cost].","Registered JSON output-entry union preserving integer values, null, and the exact string \"-inf\".","Executable reference semantics for directed walks, minimum costs, source-reachable negative cycles, and their propagation.","Registered Python checks for purity, determinism, external I/O, retained state, and standard-library-only dependencies."],"status":"unsupported_domain"}